# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Configuration
- Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` to integrate Vercel Web Analytics
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag in the root layout

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Documentation was fetched from: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Used the framework-specific instructions for Next.js App Router
- Analytics component was added to the root layout file as recommended
- Preserved all existing code structure and formatting

## Testing & Verification

✓ Build completed successfully with no errors
✓ Linter ran without issues
✓ TypeScript compilation passed
✓ All route pages generated correctly (/, /_not-found, /bolsonaro-hipotetico)

## Next Steps

To enable Web Analytics in production:
1. Deploy this project to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
3. After deployment, analytics routes will be available at `/_vercel/insights/*`

## Files Modified

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component
